   `ns_pressure_hessian_l2_bridge.lean`).  Same-window core/sheath
   cancellation only affects signed totals; total variation is additive
   over disjoint cones.

2. **Flat-radius side is NOT closeable** from existing data.  The classical
   CKN mass charge is `c r_Q²`, the radius-packing target needs `c r_Q`.
   The dyadic countermodel `r_k = 2⁻ᵏ, N_k = 2ᵏ` gives `Σ r = ∞` but
   `Σ r² < ∞`.  Interpolation/Caccioppoli pays only `r²`.  Flat-radius
   scale reserve is the SOLE remaining PDE obligation.

This section ships:
- `FlatRadiusScaleReserveSharpened` — the explicit no-log-pileup primitive
- `ClassicalCKNDataAloneFailsFlatRadiusReserve` — the in-artifact
  countermodel guard (Meta-Darwin-to-self floor-satisfiable check)
- `CriticalIncrementClosureReducedToFlatRadius` — the bundle showing
  upstream closure reduces to *one* unconstructed primitive
- `noCriticalIncrementFailure_of_reducedToFlatRadius` — the conditional
  theorem

Honest scope: this is a 1-primitive-wide reduction, NOT Clay closure and
NOT upstream closure.  The flat-radius scale-reserve theorem itself is
genuine new analytic work — not formal rearrangement.
-/

/--
Sharpened flat-radius scale-reserve primitive (tick439).

The desired theorem: for flat inherited bad nodes,
`c r_Q ≤ reserve Q − Σ_child reserve + routeSchedule + pressureVisibility +
betaIncidence`.  Telescopes to `Σ_flat r_Q < ∞`.

This is the no-log-pileup / radius-charging theorem, NOT a consequence of
existing CKN/local-energy/interpolation data.
-/
structure FlatRadiusScaleReserveSharpened (BadNode : Type u)
    [DecidableEq BadNode] where
  reserve : BadNode → Real
  reserve_nonneg : ∀ Q : BadNode, 0 ≤ reserve Q
  rootReserveBound : Real
  rootReserveBound_nonneg : 0 ≤ rootReserveBound
  radius : BadNode → Real
  radius_nonneg : ∀ Q : BadNode, 0 ≤ radius Q
  children : BadNode → Finset BadNode
  flatInheritedNode : BadNode → Prop
  routeScheduleCharge : BadNode → Real
  pressureVisibilityCharge : BadNode → Real
  betaIncidenceCharge : BadNode → Real
  radiusCoeff : Real
  radiusCoeff_pos : 0 < radiusCoeff
  flatBadScaleConsumesRadius :
    ∀ Q : BadNode,
      flatInheritedNode Q →
        radiusCoeff * radius Q ≤
          reserve Q - (children Q).sum reserve +
            routeScheduleCharge Q +
              pressureVisibilityCharge Q +
                betaIncidenceCharge Q
  telescopesToFiniteRadiusPacking : Prop
  reserveFixedBeforeBadScaleSelection : Prop
  reserveNotDerivedFromCKNSquareMass : Prop
  reserveNotDerivedFromInterpolationAlone : Prop
  reserveIsScaleSensitiveNotSpatial : Prop
  noLogPileupOrRadiusDropMechanism : Prop

/--
In-artifact countermodel guard: classical CKN/interpolation data alone
fails to produce the flat-radius scale reserve.  The dyadic countermodel
`r_k = 2⁻ᵏ, N_k = 2ᵏ` exhibits divergent `Σ r` while `Σ r² < ∞`, with the
fresh region empty when children partition the parent.

This is the Meta-Darwin-to-self floor-satisfiable-by-failing check for the
flat-radius primitive: any candidate carrier that pays only `r²` is
defeated by this countermodel.
